WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
On I go, searching for...

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
The past that was stolen from me

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Wandering on through...

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
This city, so strange to see

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.080
Choked by the scent of flames that seems to...

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.880
Cling to me

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Didn't we both say our goodbyes...

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
And go our separate ways?

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
When you see the face of hell...

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
It will squeeze your heart dry

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Fighting on seems so pointless now

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
If this must be my fate...

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Then I'll make my mind up now

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
So, please, won't you just leave me be...

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Another day

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Oh, will tomorrow hold something new to see?

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:39.460
Report: Ypsilon's personal SS-10 machine

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:44.250
was delivered to section chief Borough
on schedule at 13:03 hours. Repeat!

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:46.290
That isn't necessary.

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:48.170
Damn Borough.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:51.420
His ridiculous experiments are eating up
nearly all our resources.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.250
The experiments have their purpose.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:55.750
Your Excellency must realize that as well.

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:57.710
Well, Gurran.

00:01:57.710 --> 00:01:59.540
Do you think they can both make it back safely?

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:05.460
Yes. However, we're still betting that Ypsilon
will be able to steal Proto One back.

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:07.290
We don't need Proto One.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:11.710
No, we do. I wish to see her again.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:14.960
You met her only once
before we sent her to Kummen.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:19.750
Are you in love with her, Arron?

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:24.460
Of course not. She interests me
only as an experimental subject.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.040
Soon the results will be known.

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:32.920
The civil war in Kummen will be at an end.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:36.250
Though it's certainly become
a rather noisy end, hasn't it?

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:47.420
Dark Change

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:20.830
If you're going to kill me, then kill me!

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:24.460
I will, once I'm finished with you.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:26.000
What do you want?

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.960
For you to answer my questions.

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:31.380
That would depend on what they are.

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:35.380
Why did you bring her and Ypsilon here?

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:47.210
To experiment on them!

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:48.540
Experiment?

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:50.960
Then the PS's still haven't been perfected?

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:52.920
Why do you want to know?

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.170
All right! Don't shoot!

00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:07.380
It was for psychological testing!

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:12.710
The PS's body systems have been
perfected but not their minds.

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:15.330
We were trying to merge emotions
with their battle skills.

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:16.380
What was the result?

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:20.960
We learned both PS's, Proto One
and Ypsilon, are incomplete.

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:21.960
Why?

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.920
Because they're still dominated
by human emotions.

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:28.750
To be effective weapons,
they must possess pure hatred.

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:30.250
Satisfied, Chirico?

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:34.420
Ypsilon!

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.460
Is that your new custom machine?

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:42.500
I may not be a perfect PS,
but my machine is perfect!

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:43.670
Wait!

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:45.040
Are you afraid?

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:47.040
I still have questions.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.250
Haven't you contacted Kan Yu yet?

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:47.040
No response at all, sir.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:50.330
Damned fool!
He couldn't have gotten himself killed!

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:53.580
Forget the small fries! Go in as deep as you can!

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:02.380
Our forces are breaking in.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:03.830
I know that!

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:05.080
Aren't we going to join up with them?

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:08.830
Like this? I can't show my face
until I get that PS back!

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:12.500
I'll cover you! Go on ahead, Shako! Go!

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.630
What are you waiting for, Ypsilon! Kill him!

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:32.830
One last question.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:40.420
Borough, can a PS be turned back
into a normal human?

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:43.630
Well?

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:45.250
It's impossible!

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:47.330
They can't be made normal again!

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:57.000
Chirico, prepare yourself!

00:06:58.170 --> 00:06:59.920
Stop it, Ypsilon!

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:05.040
Don't move, Chirico.

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:06.170
Kiderra?

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:11.040
I'm right behind him. I'll teach him a thing or two.

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:13.750
Don't! He knows you're there!

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:16.920
Like hell he does.
I'm not that clumsy. Here goes!

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:17.580
No!

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:28.250
Kiderra!

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:39.130
Guess you'll never get to
pay me back, huh, Chirico?

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:47.040
Kiderra!

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:49.790
Chirico!

00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:22.630
Stop it, Ypsilon!

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:26.460
Just be quiet and watch!

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:41.500
This is Borough. How's the battle going?

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:43.540
We can't stop their advance.

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:45.540
Send Ypsilon out now!

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:46.670
Where's the prince?

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:49.080
Killed by the enemy, sir!

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:52.210
Borough here! Is the escape shuttle ready?

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:53.380
All set, sir.

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:56.500
All right! We'll leave as soon as
Ypsilon kills Chirico!

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:06.920
This way.

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:39.960
A message from Captain Kan Yu, sir!

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:42.790
I've cornered the PS!

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:44.630
What? Really?

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:46.330
They're beneath the villa!

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:48.420
Good work! We're on our way!

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:52.710
To all units: the target is beneath the villa.

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:53.790
Attack!

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:55.290
Take us down.

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:11.580
General Battentain,
we'll be arriving in ten minutes.

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:14.330
The Kummen rebels will be
destroyed in one hour

00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:17.080
and the PS will be back in our hands.

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:19.040
What about the mercenaries' movements?

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:22.040
Their commander, Gon Nu,
seems to have accepted our offer.

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:23.500
Is there a problem?

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:24.790
Perhaps.

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:28.040
The Kummen government seems to not want them
around after the rebels have been put down.

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:30.420
The final conclusion of our secret talks, eh?

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:35.250
They consider them an impediment to security
and national consolidation in a post-war Kummen.

00:10:35.750 --> 00:10:36.790
I see.

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:39.790
They have no place in a peaceful Kummen.

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:41.420
They only know how to destroy.

00:10:41.420 --> 00:10:43.880
Do you understand what I'm telling you, Captain?

00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:45.880
Just leave everything to me, sir.

00:11:02.460 --> 00:11:04.580
I think we got far enough away to be safe.

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:06.250
Where's Chirico?

00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:08.420
Probably fighting the PS.

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:11.880
Gon Nu's after the PS, too.
He might try to kill Chirico!

00:11:13.130 --> 00:11:15.250
Never mind me. Go help Chirico!

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:16.500
But...!

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:19.130
The prince gave me something. Take it!

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:14.040
God dammit!

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:19.380
This is jijirium.

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:24.880
So, they weren't just experimenting.
They wanted to make more PS's!

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:33.790
Soon Chirico will be dead.

00:12:37.210 --> 00:12:39.460
No, you fool! Stay in the machine!

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:44.750
I'll finish him with my bare hands!

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:46.580
Come out, Chirico!

00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:54.500
Come out, Chirico!

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:57.000
I know you won't run. Come out!

00:13:08.540 --> 00:13:11.250
A duel? How noble of you.

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:20.380
Stop it, Ypsilon!

00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:23.750
I won't let you hurt Chirico!

00:13:25.460 --> 00:13:27.380
You can't shoot me.

00:13:27.380 --> 00:13:29.790
I can! I love him!

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:32.130
You can't shoot me!

00:13:35.130 --> 00:13:36.670
Don't move, Ypsilon!

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:40.580
Stop it, Ypsilon!

00:13:42.580 --> 00:13:43.750
Stop it!

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:55.750
Ypsilon...

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:19.380
Who will win? Chirico or the PS?

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:23.000
Whichever one does, there is no escape!

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:25.670
Surrender! You have no choice now!

00:14:31.630 --> 00:14:34.500
What'll you do? Answer me, or we'll attack!

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:36.830
Prepare to launch!

00:14:36.830 --> 00:14:37.830
Yes, sir!

00:14:40.670 --> 00:14:42.000
What's happening?

00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:45.830
Melkian soldiers, sir!

00:14:45.830 --> 00:14:48.290
Lots of them are attacking!

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:49.960
Rochina's come?

00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:11.250
AT forces, drop!

00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:13.210
Kill any armed personnel on sight!

00:16:18.630 --> 00:16:21.420
What's going on? This wasn't in the deal!

00:16:21.420 --> 00:16:24.000
They said they'd make me a Melkian officer
in exchange for the PS!

00:16:34.170 --> 00:16:37.000
Ypsilon! What are you doing, Ypsilon?

00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:39.460
We have to escape! Hurry!

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:06.500
Uh-oh!

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:29.750
Hah! Idiots!

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:53.630
Hey! Chirico! Over here! Hey!

00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:56.790
Vanilla!

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:32.250
So, this is Prince Kanjelman's escape shuttle.

00:18:32.830 --> 00:18:35.000
He hasn't escaped yet?

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:36.920
Guess he didn't want to.

00:18:37.670 --> 00:18:40.380
Actually, he can't now.

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:44.830
He gave the key to Potaria just before he died.

00:18:44.830 --> 00:18:46.330
Potaria said to give it to you.

00:18:46.330 --> 00:18:48.210
But it's a one-seater.

00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:49.880
Only one person can escape.

00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:54.250
There's a PS capsule mounted in the ammo bay.

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:57.880
I see. Borough was going to
escape with Ypsilon in it.

00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:01.040
Good news. Now hurry up and get in.

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:03.040
What are you saying? What about you?

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:05.250
What are you talking about?

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:07.330
They're only after you guys.

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:09.380
They ain't gonna be able to catch me.

00:19:09.880 --> 00:19:11.000
Vanilla...

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:13.630
Don't forget, I'll be sending you a bill later.

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:16.580
But in the meantime you can enjoy
a nice honeymoon up in orbit.

00:19:23.290 --> 00:19:26.380
I will, of course, be charging interest, too.

00:19:26.380 --> 00:19:28.790
I'm sorry, but you're staying here.

00:19:33.630 --> 00:19:36.290
You idiot! The Melkians are attacking now!

00:19:36.290 --> 00:19:38.290
You're in as much danger as we are!

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:40.170
Chirico, get going!

00:19:40.170 --> 00:19:44.170
Once I have you, I can defect to the Melkians
and hand you over as part of the deal.

00:19:44.170 --> 00:19:46.330
If that doesn't work, I'll blow this place up!

00:19:46.710 --> 00:19:49.880
If anyone here even twitches, they die!

00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:57.420
You son of a...! What are you doing?

00:19:57.420 --> 00:19:59.000
Turning against your superior officer, huh?

00:19:59.710 --> 00:20:01.420
You bastard!

00:20:06.960 --> 00:20:09.460
You are human scum!

00:20:41.380 --> 00:20:44.330
Is there any point in surviving?

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:45.540
Stop that.

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:50.000
I'm a PS. I can never be a normal human again.

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:52.330
That's not true. Borough was lying!

00:20:52.330 --> 00:20:54.170
Fyana, some day...

00:21:05.920 --> 00:21:07.080
Chirico...

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:32.580
Chirico, move it!

00:21:32.830 --> 00:21:34.460
Till next time, Vanilla!

00:22:08.080 --> 00:22:10.460
Thanks for your help.

00:22:10.460 --> 00:22:11.790
Forget it.

00:22:12.080 --> 00:22:14.540
Now then, shall we get the hell out of here?

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:22.080
Yeah, right. I've got Coconna waiting for me.

00:22:22.080 --> 00:22:24.710
Can't get myself killed just yet.

00:22:25.630 --> 00:22:27.670
Say, do you have a girlfriend, too?

00:22:36.830 --> 00:22:39.000
My journey through Kummen was at an end.

00:22:39.830 --> 00:22:42.420
For my own sake, I had chosen to enter Hell.

00:22:42.750 --> 00:22:44.710
For Fyana's sake, I was now leaving it behind.

00:22:45.790 --> 00:22:46.790
Love...?

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:51.750
Could it be even I was capable
of fighting for love?

00:22:53.330 --> 00:22:54.750
Next Episode

00:22:54.830 --> 00:22:57.790
It all began in the darkness of Lido.

00:22:57.790 --> 00:23:00.130
People are born. People die.

00:23:00.130 --> 00:23:03.210
If there is a path to Heaven,
then people’s lives must be governed by fate.

00:23:03.420 --> 00:23:07.790
When pursued by flames and driven
toward conflict, where do we finally arrive?

00:23:07.790 --> 00:23:11.210
Moreover, what must one seek in this life?

00:23:11.210 --> 00:23:12.790
For what should we strive?

00:23:12.790 --> 00:23:14.210
Who must be struck down...

00:23:14.210 --> 00:23:16.880
And what, exactly, am "I"?

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:18.830
Next time, "Destiny"

00:23:18.830 --> 00:23:23.290
Destiny

00:23:18.830 --> 00:23:23.290
Next Time

00:23:18.840 --> 00:23:22.000
Taking no heed, Chirico charges
through the destruction.

00:23:41.540 --> 00:23:45.040
Whenever I'm feeling lonely

00:23:45.040 --> 00:23:48.540
Whenever I'm feeling sad

00:23:48.540 --> 00:23:54.960
I can always see you floating in my mind

00:23:55.420 --> 00:23:58.960
Whenever I'm alone

00:23:58.960 --> 00:24:02.420
Whenever I long for you

00:24:02.420 --> 00:24:08.670
I can always feel you inside my heart

00:24:08.670 --> 00:24:12.170
No matter how far apart we may go

00:24:12.170 --> 00:24:15.540
No matter if my path should part from yours

00:24:15.750 --> 00:24:22.040
The memories of you seem to shine inside my heart...

00:24:22.460 --> 00:24:28.420
Brighter than any other light...
